## FAQ

### What equipment do I need for a virtual event?

You need in-room sound so people can hear the call, a screen or display so they can see it, and a way to connect your laptop to both. Our [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) covers all three with HDMI and USB-C adapters included.

### How much does audio visual rental cost for a virtual event?

Pricing depends on the package: our full catalog, from the Product Presentation Pack up to the MICE Pack for a larger conference room, is listed with exact euro pricing on our [packages page](/packages/). All rates are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout, and every price includes delivery, setup and teardown.

### What is the difference between a virtual event and a hybrid event?

A fully virtual event has no in-person audience at all. A hybrid event has both an in-person room and remote participants on a call. Either way, we supply the same thing: the room's sound, screen and laptop connectivity. See [What We Provide vs. What You Bring](#what-we-provide-vs-what-you-bring) above.

### Can I connect my own laptop to your sound and screen setup?

Yes. The [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) includes HDMI and USB-C adapters plus audio interfaces to connect your laptop, tablet or media player.

### Do you provide cameras or streaming equipment?

No. We provide the room's sound and screen, not cameras, streaming encoders or a recording service. You run the call from your own laptop and software.

### Do you provide internet or wifi for the event?

No, internet and wifi are not part of our packages. Confirm connectivity with your venue before the event.

### Do I need an on-site AV technician?

Not on every package. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a technician on site for up to six hours; on other packages a technician is available as an add on. Ask when you book.

### How many people can your equipment support?

It scales with the package: the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) covers up to 40 guests, and the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers up to 120. See the full comparison on our [packages page](/packages/).
